## Phase 2 — Feature Menu

**IMPORTANT:** The user wants to implement these one at a time. At the start of each session,
present this list and ask which feature to work on. Do not begin implementing until the user
confirms their choice.

### P2-1: UK Bank Holidays & Special Days
- Add a `holidays.js` module with UK bank holidays for the current and next year, plus recurring
  special days (Easter, Christmas, Boxing Day, New Year's Day, etc.)
- Easter date calculation needed (Butcher/Meeus algorithm)
- In `buildCardHTML()` and `renderExpandedEvents()`, show a small badge on relevant dates
- Settings toggle: "Show bank holidays" (on by default)

### P2-2: Colour Themes for Days
- Extend the `theme` setting (currently `'light'`/`'dark'`) to support named colour themes
  (e.g. `'blue'`, `'warm'`, `'high-contrast'`)
- Define CSS variable overrides per theme in `base.css` (`body.theme-blue { --day-card-bg: …; }`)
- Add theme picker to settings dropdown (colour swatches row)

### P2-3: Full-Text Search
- Replace the "Search coming in a future update" stub in `openSearch()` with real search
- Search across: diary text (strip HTML tags), event/todo/reminder titles and notes
- Results list: date, type badge, matching snippet — tap result → navigate to that week and
  open expanded day
- Debounce input (300ms), case-insensitive

### P2-4: Repeat Events — Full Implementation
- `addEvent()` already stores a `repeat` field (`null | 'daily' | 'weekly' | 'monthly' | 'yearly'`)
  but doesn't expand it
- When rendering a week, generate virtual events from repeat rules (compute on the fly from the
  template event on its original date — don't store per-day copies)
- Editing a repeated event: prompt "Edit this occurrence / Edit all future / Edit all"

### P2-5: System Notifications for Reminders
- Use the Notifications API (request permission on first use, surfaced in settings)
- On app load and at midnight refresh, register `setTimeout` calls for any event with
  `reminderMinutes` set that falls within the next 24 h
- Show a native notification with the event title and time

### P2-6: iCal / .ics Export
- In `handleSettingsAction('export')`, offer a second option: "Export iCal (.ics)"
- Build an `.ics` string from all events with proper VEVENT blocks (DTSTART, DTEND, SUMMARY, UID)

### P2-7: Google Calendar Sync
- Authenticate via Google OAuth 2.0 (PKCE flow for a web app)
- Sync events to/from Google Calendar; show last-sync time in settings
- Scaffold the auth flow first with the Google API client library loaded from CDN

### P2-8: Day Navigation in Expanded View
- Add prev/next day buttons (chevron arrows) to the expanded day overlay header
- Tapping navigates to the adjacent day, updating the week grid if the week changes

### P2-9: Mood Tags
- Add a mood selector (emoji row: 😊 😐 😔 😤 😴) to the expanded day view
- Store as `days[dateKey].mood`
- Show a small mood indicator on the day card

---

## Key Patterns & Conventions

- **No build step** — plain ES module `<script type="module" src="js/app.js">`. All imports are relative.
- **State** lives in `app.js`: `state.data` (the JSON model), `state.today`, `state.currentWeekStart`.
- **Save** = `saveData()` → `localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(state.data))`.
- **Modals** push a `history.pushState` on open; close via `history.back()`. The `popstate` handler
  in `init()` dispatches to the right close function.
- **No inline comments explaining WHAT the code does** — only add a comment if the WHY is non-obvious.
- **No emojis** in UI text (emojis used as icons only where already present, e.g. 🔔 for reminder).
- **CSS variables** defined in `base.css` `:root` and `body.dark`. Use them everywhere.
- **`esc(str)`** — always escape user content before inserting into innerHTML.
- **Gestures** — `gestures.js` handles long-press on the week grid using touch events only.
  Do not add competing pointer/touch listeners at the grid level.
- The format toolbar is a **singleton** — one instance attached to `document.body`, shared across
  all diary areas.
- **Mobile first** — use touch events (`touchstart`/`touchend`) for any interactive gesture;
  pointer events alone are unreliable on Android (browser can fire `pointercancel`).
